; Tutorial_4_Edit_and_Add_Records.inix -- changing a record and adding one.

[about]
Title=4 - Edit and Add Records
Intro=JobTrail, the job-search template, opened; then a cell edited with F2, a value picked from a list with Control plus F2, and a new record added with Control plus N.
Setup=DbDo is open; this walk opens JobTrail.
Homework=Add a record of your own and fill three of its fields.

[step]

Say=One want: one job's status brought up to date, and a new job added.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=JobTrail comes next: a template for a job search, whose jobs, employers and contacts are linked to one another, so it shows more of what DbDo can do. Alt plus Shift plus D, D for Database, opens a template.
Key=Alt+Shift+D
Hear=Template Databases dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose JobTrail and press Enter. Shift plus Z says where I am.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=jobs, 12 records, no filter, sorted by employer
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I move to the status column of the record to change. F2 edits the cell under the cursor, as F2 renames a file in Windows.
Key=F2
Hear=status: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type the new value and press Enter to keep it.
Key=Enter
Hear=(the record, with its new status)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Where a field has fixed values, Control plus F2 edits by picking one, so nothing is mistyped.
Key=Control+F2
Hear=status: list box
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow to the value, and Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=(the record, with the picked status)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus N, N for New, adds a record to the table, and focus goes to its first field.
Key=Control+N
Hear=New record
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I fill each field with F2 as before. Shift plus A, A for Added, says when this record was added.
Key=Shift+A
Hear=(the date and time the record was added)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: Control plus D deletes a record, D for Delete, and asks first. Escape answers no.
Key=Control+D
Hear=Delete this record? No button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape keeps it.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Notes hold whatever does not fit a column. Alt plus Shift plus N, Edit Notes, opens this record's notes in a box of their own.
Key=Alt+Shift+N
Hear=Notes: edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type a line about the interview, and Control plus Enter keeps it. Shift plus N says the notes back.
Key=Shift+N
Hear=Second interview Tuesday at ten.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Tags work the same way, with Alt plus Shift plus T to edit and Shift plus T to hear them: words such as remote or referral, to filter by later.
Key=Shift+T
Hear=remote, referral
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus E, Say Edited, says when this record last changed, so a stale one is easy to spot.
Key=Shift+E
Hear=Edited today at 3:42 PM
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus C, Copy Record, adds a copy of this record as a new one: quicker than typing a second job at the same employer.
Key=Control+Shift+C
Hear=Record copied
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus R, Replace Column, finds and replaces text in the column I am on, in every record, for a name spelled two ways.
Key=Control+R
Hear=Replace Column dialog, Find: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, for now. A replacement counts what it changed and says so.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A record can carry a web address, such as a job posting. Alt plus Shift plus U, Edit URL, edits it.
Key=Alt+Shift+U
Hear=url: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter keeps it. Shift plus U says it back, and Control plus Shift plus U opens it in the browser.
Key=Shift+U
Hear=https colon slash slash jobs dot example dot com slash 4821
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Edit the cell I am on.
Key=
Hear=F2

[step]

Say=Edit by picking a value.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F2

[step]

Say=Add a record.
Key=
Hear=Control plus N
